WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:04.890
How do you speak truth to power when you work in an environment where

00:00:04.890 --> 00:00:09.330
speaking truth to power can get you fired or
could get you in trouble?

00:00:09.330 --> 00:00:10.444
One of the reasons that happens

00:00:10.444 --> 00:00:12.240
is not because we're necessarily
"speaking truth to power"

00:00:12.240 --> 00:00:14.200
it's the manner in which we do it.

00:00:14.200 --> 00:00:16.000
We usually do it as a complaint

00:00:16.000 --> 00:00:17.400
or we do it as an aggressive question

00:00:17.400 --> 00:00:19.100
and we also do it without empathy.

00:00:19.100 --> 00:00:20.200
One of the most important things to do is

00:00:20.200 --> 00:00:22.700
have empathy for the people who we work for.

00:00:22.700 --> 00:00:25.000
We don't know what their story is,

00:00:25.000 --> 00:00:26.849
we don't know what kind of pressure they're under,

00:00:26.849 --> 00:00:30.300
we don't know if they're operating from a point 
of fear.

00:00:30.300 --> 00:00:32.900
And so when we come in guns blazing

00:00:32.900 --> 00:00:35.400
their walls are gonna go up

00:00:35.400 --> 00:00:38.960
because we're aggressive or we're
perceived as aggressive.

00:00:38.960 --> 00:00:44.930
So if you can maintain empathy 
and some curiosity

00:00:44.930 --> 00:00:48.067
and work hard to spend the time to 
build a relationship

00:00:48.067 --> 00:00:51.500
with that person in that authority position

00:00:51.500 --> 00:00:55.400
so they understand that we want to 
see them succeed.

00:00:55.400 --> 00:00:56.891
And I want to ask you some
questions

00:00:56.891 --> 00:00:58.140
because if you can answer these questions

00:00:58.140 --> 00:01:01.600
I can be more successful,
which is gonna help you be more successful.

00:01:01.600 --> 00:01:03.900
Or to say things like, 
"Are you OK?"

00:01:03.900 --> 00:01:07.300
Or to say things like, 
"Hey, you were really harsh to us in the meeting today,

00:01:07.300 --> 00:01:08.400
I just want to check in with you.

00:01:08.400 --> 00:01:09.640
Is everything okay?"

00:01:09.640 --> 00:01:12.180
These are little things
we can do to think about them as human beings

00:01:12.180 --> 00:01:15.000
rather than oppressors

00:01:15.000 --> 00:01:17.600
and to operate with as much empathy and curiosity 
as possible

00:01:17.600 --> 00:01:19.283
and hopefully build that relationship

00:01:19.283 --> 00:01:21.278
so they see us as trusted and trusting

00:01:21.278 --> 00:01:23.314
and amazingly they'll probably open up

00:01:23.314 --> 00:01:26.800
and you'll learn a lot more so, that works.

